  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "src/features/diskBrowser/composables/useDiskBrowser.ts",
      "content": "The implementation was changed to `async ...: Promise\u003cvoid\u003e`, but the exported return-type contract still declares `toggleFavorite: (folderPath: string) =\u003e void`. `toggleFavorite` is now invoked directly from Vue event handlers (`@toggle-favorite=\"toggleFavorite\"`, `@remove-favorite=\"toggleFavorite\"`) without `await`/`void`, so a rejected promise (e.g. an error thrown outside the internal try block, like the rollback assignment or showMessage) would surface as an unhandled rejection. Please update the declared type to `(folderPath: string) =\u003e Promise\u003cvoid\u003e` so the contract matches the implementation and callers are aware it is async.",
      "suggestion_code": "  toggleFavorite: (folderPath: string) =\u003e Promise\u003cvoid\u003e",
      "existing_code": "  toggleFavorite: (folderPath: string) =\u003e void",
      "start_line": 48,
      "end_line": 48,
      "category": "maintainability",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/features/diskBrowser/composables/useDiskBrowser.ts",
      "content": "`toggleFavorite` now does an optimistic in-place mutation then persists asynchronously. On save failure it rolls back with `favoriteFolders.value = previous`. Since `favoriteFolders` is a plain `ref`, reassignment works, but the rollback is not concurrency-safe: two rapid toggle clicks can interleave, so a failed save for the first click can clobber the second click's state (and vice versa), leaving the UI out of sync with storage. Consider serializing the saves (e.g. a simple in-flight guard) or disabling the toggle button while a save is pending.",
      "existing_code": "    } catch (error) {\n      favoriteFolders.value = previous\n      console.error(\"保存收藏夹失败:\", error)\n      showMessage(i18n.favoriteSaveFailed!, 3000, \"error\")\n    }",
      "start_line": 117,
      "end_line": 121,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/features/diskBrowser/utils/index.ts",
      "content": "The i18n-fallback removal was applied only partially. `formatDate` now uses non-null assertions (`i18n.today!`, `i18n.daysAgo!`), but `computeCacheStatus` a few lines above still uses hardcoded fallbacks (`i18n.cacheExpired || \"缓存已过期\"`, `i18n.minutesRemaining || \"分钟\"`, the `缓存有效期剩余 ...` template, etc.). This leaves the module with two contradictory i18n conventions after the refactor, which is confusing and defeats the goal of eliminating hardcoded fallbacks. Align the rest of the file to a single convention.",
      "existing_code": "    text: labelType === \"full\" ? i18n.cacheExpired || \"缓存已过期\" : i18n.expired || \"已过期\",\n      isExpired: true,\n      tooltip: i18n.cacheExpiredTooltip || \"缓存已过期，点击刷新按钮获取最新数据\",",
      "start_line": 133,
      "end_line": 135,
      "category": "maintainability",
      "severity": "medium"
    }
  ],
